# parser-clang.patch — Clang __builtin_riscv_prs_* for the rtl-fun parser extension
# (Phase 7 C1 + C3, light path: builtin -> prs.* inline asm). Applied to clang-unwrapped
# (sourceRoot = <src>/clang) by nix/parser-clang.nix; MC support comes from the linked
# parser-patched libLLVM (C0), so this patch touches ONLY clang/ files:
#   include/clang/Basic/BuiltinsRISCV.td          (+1 include hook)
#   include/clang/Basic/BuiltinsRISCVXparser.td   (GENERATED decls — do not hand-edit)
#   include/clang/Basic/parser-clang-builtins.inc (GENERATED X-macro tables — likewise)
#   lib/Sema/SemaRISCV.cpp                         (+ generic immediate-range arm)
#   lib/CodeGen/TargetBuiltins/RISCV.cpp          (+ InlineAsm.h + two generic lowering arms:
#                                                   C0 immediate + C3 register-move)
# C1 = 67 immediate-only custom-0 builtins (void, `i` operands). C3 = the 4 custom-3
# register moves (prs.mv.x.p/mv.p.x/cam.read/array.read): the p-register is a _Constant
# baked into the mnemonic as `p<N>`, the GPRs are real `=r`/`r` operands, reads return a
# value. The GENERATED files are emitted by tools/parser-gen into toolchain/generated and
# re-pasted here; parser-gen-check guards the toolchain/generated copies byte-stable.
#
